SDL2.LIBRARY					53.23	26.10.2026 based on SDL 2.32.11
SDL2_IMAGE.LIBRARY		53.7	06.10.2026 based on SDL2_IMAGE 2.8.13
SDL2_MIXER.LIBRARY		53.8	06.10.2026 based on SDL2_MIXER 2.8.2
SDL2_TTF.LIBRARY			53.10	06.10.2026 based on SDL2_TTF 2.25.0
SDL2_NET.LIBRARY			53.3	04.06.2026 based on SDL2_NET 2.4.0
SDL2_GFX.LIBRARY			53.1	04.06.2026 based on SDL2_GFX 1.0.4

Simple DirectMedia Layer
************************

What is it?
Simple DirectMedia Layer is a cross-platform development library designed to provide low level access to audio, keyboard, mouse, joystick, and graphics hardware via OpenGL/Direct3D/Metal/Vulkan. It is used by video playback software, emulators, and popular games including Valve's award winning catalog and many Humble Bundle games.

SDL 2.0 is distributed under the zlib license. This license allows you to use SDL freely in any software.

https://libsdl.org/
https://wiki.libsdl.org/


Installation:
*************

MorphOS version 3.20 is required to be installed as a minimum.
Developer: You need  new SDK 3.20!!
sdl2_ttf.library needs freetype.library 59 and harfbuzz.library 67 (system libraries).
sdl2_image.library uses system jfif.library, png.library and tiff.library, sdl2_mixer.library uses vorbisfile.library (optional).

Just double-click on the Install icon and read the incremental instructions.

- WARNING: it's recommended that you have a minimum 64MB graphics video (opengl features)
(if not, then it is advised that you disable "enhanced display" and reduce your screen resolution of Ambient)


SDL2 MorphOS Features:
**********************

- SDL2 support ALTIVEC
- SDL2 working with non-3D system (Qemu for exemple), using SOFTWARE renderer
- SDL renderer: OpenGL, Overlay (cgxvideo VLayer, SDL_RENDER_DRIVER=overlay) and Software renderer are available
- Joystick support for sensors.library - Most compatible with the Xbox360 controller (or hardware recognised as that controller type)
- Joystick HotPlug supported

SDL2 MorphOS specific and limitation:
************************************

- SDL_GetBasePath: \WARNING/ return a full absolute path unless path separator (/) at end
- Do not use SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN on SDL_CreateWindow. This flags doesnt create the window intuition immediately.

GameController Readme:
**********************

You can create your own mapping file for any joystick (gamecontrollerdb.txt) : check directory controller map
Specific to MorphOS, you can put this file in your ENVARC. Then any game can use it! Then there's no need to put this file in indiviual game directories.

A MorphOS community sourced database of game controller mappings can be used that have SDL2 Game Controller functionality,
which is available here : https://github.com/BeWorld2018/gamecontrollerdb.txt

Please don't hesitate to participate in adding to this database, so kindly send me your working mapping(s) to add to our database. Thanks !

